sentences.text:
10. Accordingly, the appeal merits consideration, in the result the following:
ORDER (i) The appeal is allowed;
(ii) The impugned judgment and award is set aside;
(iii) The matter is remanded back to the Tribunal to the stage of further evidence of the parties;
(iv) The Tribunal is requested to afford an opportunity to the insurance company to implead the owner and insurer of the tempo traveler also afford opportunity to both parties to lead additional evidence and then to adjudicate the claim on merits in accordance with law;
(v) Without further notice, the parties shall appear before the Tribunal on 30.09.2024;
(vi) As the accident is of the year 2011, the Tribunal is directed to dispose of the claim petition within 6 months from the date of receipt of certified copy of this order;
NC: 2024:KHC:37347 (vii) The office shall transmit the TCR along with copy of this order to the Tribunal forthwith.

